<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>MAMA CLI — APT repository</title>
<meta name="description" content="Install mama, your Telugu-speaking terminal buddy, with apt.">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf8;
    --fg: #23201c;
    --muted: #6b645c;
    --rule: #e3ded7;
    --code-bg: #f3f0ec;
    --accent: #0e7490;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg: #171614;
      --fg: #eceae6;
      --muted: #a09991;
      --rule: #302d29;
      --code-bg: #211f1c;
      --accent: #67c5d8;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
    font: 16px/1.65 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  }
  main { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 16px 6rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .tagline { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  h2 {
    font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .09em;
    color: var(--muted); margin: 2.75rem 0 .75rem; font-weight: 600;
  }
  pre {
    background: var(--code-bg); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem; overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font: 13px/1.6 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }
  p code { background: var(--code-bg); padding: .1em .35em; border-radius: 4px; font-size: .9em; }
  .sample {
    background: var(--code-bg); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem; white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font: 14px/1.7 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  footer {
    margin-top: 3.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--muted); font-size: .875rem;
  }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  li { margin: .3rem 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>MAMA CLI</h1>
  <p class="tagline">ni terminal mama — your Telugu-speaking terminal buddy.</p>

  <div class="sample">$ mama

mama ❤️

"nemmadiga veltunnavani badhapadaku mama,
 agipoleduga... ade mukhyam."

— ni terminal mama 😎</div>

  <h2>Install on Debian or Ubuntu</h2>
  <p>Add the repository once:</p>
<pre><code>sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL @PAGES_URL@/@KEY_FILE@ \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/keyrings/mama.asc &gt; /dev/null

echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/mama.asc] @PAGES_URL@ @SUITE@ @COMPONENT@" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/mama.list &gt; /dev/null

sudo apt update</code></pre>

  <p>Then, now and for every future version:</p>
<pre><code>sudo apt install mama</code></pre>

  <h2>Use it</h2>
<pre><code>mama              # random Telugu wisdom
mama motivate     # motivation
mama calm         # slow down
mama morning      # start of day
mama night        # end of day
mama code         # developer wisdom
mama git          # git humour
mama roast        # roast your terminal
mama coffee       # coffee wisdom
mama friday       # weekend mode

man mama          # the full manual</code></pre>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Node.js 18+</strong> — apt installs the <code>nodejs</code> package for you.</li>
    <li><strong>A UTF-8 terminal</strong>, for the emoji. Messages are Telugu
      written in Latin letters, so there is no font to install and nothing to
      configure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Without the repository</h2>
  <p>You can also install a single <code>.deb</code> directly:</p>
<pre><code>wget @PAGES_URL@/pool/@COMPONENT@/m/mama/mama_@VERSION@_all.deb
sudo apt install ./mama_@VERSION@_all.deb</code></pre>

  <h2>Uninstall</h2>
<pre><code>sudo apt remove mama
sudo rm /etc/apt/sources.list.d/mama.list /etc/apt/keyrings/mama.asc</code></pre>

  <footer>
    <p>MAMA is a humour utility. It never executes commands, modifies your
    files or git repositories, or makes network requests — a message may
    <em>contain</em> text like a git command, but it is only ever printed.</p>
    <p>Source and issues:
      <a href="https://github.com/@OWNER@/@REPO@">github.com/@OWNER@/@REPO@</a>
      · MIT licensed</p>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
